{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>The seventh week.</b> As its Targum renders: the seventh week." "<b>Until the morrow of the seventh week you shall count.</b> And not inclusive — and they are forty-nine days." "<b>Fifty days and you shall bring a new meal-offering to YHWH.</b> On the fiftieth day you shall bring it. And I say this is its midrash, but its plain sense is: until the morrow of the seventh week, which is the fiftieth day, you shall count — and it is an inverted verse." "<b>A new meal-offering.</b> It is the first meal-offering brought from the new grain. And if you say: but the meal-offering of the Omer was already brought — it is not like all other meal-offerings, for it comes from barley (Menachot 14)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:55.515329211Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}